# Build-context ignore for deploy/azure/Dockerfile (source build).
#
# BuildKit uses "<dockerfile>.dockerignore" when present, so this applies
# ONLY to `docker build -f deploy/azure/Dockerfile .` and does not affect the
# repo-root .dockerignore used by the published-image Dockerfile.
#
# Unlike the root .dockerignore, this MUST keep scripts/ (build:universal-
# package runs scripts/createUniversalPackage.ts) and tests/ (tests/browser is
# a pnpm workspace member required by --frozen-lockfile). It only strips
# things that are rebuilt or irrelevant to the build.

# Dependencies and build outputs are reinstalled / rebuilt inside the image.
node_modules
**/node_modules
dist
**/dist
coverage
**/coverage

# VCS, local state, secrets, logs.
.git
.gitignore
.env
*.env
*.log
tmp
**/tmp
.vscode
.idea

# Container assets and docs not needed to compile.
**/*.Dockerfile
Dockerfile
deploy/aws
*.md
**/*.md

# Local X.509 fixtures / certs must never enter an image build context.
*.pem
**/*.pem
